    <name>
      <text>real-life-sequence-q2</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A learner in a Junior School saves money every week. Each week she saves Ksh {@dv@} more than in the week before, so the weekly savings form an arithmetic progression (AP).</p>
<p>The amounts she saves in week 1, week 4 and week 8 are the first three terms of a geometric progression (GP).</p>


<p>(a) Find the amount she saves in week 1, in Ksh.</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p>(b) Find the common ratio of the GP.</p>
<p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>(c) The GP continues for 4 terms. Find the sum of the first 4 terms of the GP, in Ksh.</p>
<p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>

<p>(d) Find the total amount she saves in the first 8 weeks, in Ksh.</p>
<p>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The AP has common difference \( d = {@dv@} \). The 1st, 4th and 8th terms are \( a \), \( a + 3d \) and \( a + 7d \).</p>

<p>(a) <strong>First term:</strong></p>
<p>These three terms form a GP, so the ratio between neighbouring terms is the same:</p>
<p>\[ \frac{a + 3d}{a} = \frac{a + 7d}{a + 3d} \quad \text{so} \quad (a + 3d)^2 = a(a + 7d) \]</p>
<p>Expand both sides:</p>
<p>\[ a^2 + 6ad + 9d^2 = a^2 + 7ad \]</p>
<p>The \(a^2\) terms cancel. Collect the other terms:</p>
<p>\[ 9d^2 = ad \]</p>
<p>Divide both sides by \(d\):</p>
<p>\[ a = 9d = 9 \times {@dv@} = {@ta1@} \]</p>
<p>She saves Ksh {@ta1@} in week 1.</p>

<p>(b) <strong>Common ratio:</strong></p>
<p>Week 4: \( {@a@} + 3 \times {@dv@} = {@t4@} \). Week 8: \( {@a@} + 7 \times {@dv@} = {@t8@} \).</p>
<p>\[ r = \frac{ {@t4@} }{ {@a@} } = {@ta2@} \]</p>
<p>Check: \( \frac{ {@t8@} }{ {@t4@} } = {@ta2@} \).</p>

<p>(c) <strong>Sum of the first 4 terms of the GP:</strong></p>
<p>\[ S_4 = \frac{ {@a@}\left(\left({@r@}\right)^4 - 1\right)}{ {@r@} - 1 } = {@ta3@} \]</p>
<p>The sum is Ksh {@ta3@}.</p>

<p>(d) <strong>First 8 weeks:</strong></p>
<p>The weekly savings form the AP, so use the AP sum formula:</p>
<p>\[ S_8 = \frac{8}{2}\left(2 \times {@a@} + 7 \times {@dv@}\right) = 4 \times {@2*a + 7*dv@} = {@ta4@} \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
